### S-live-holder: a live holder keeps the queue lock past the 1s deadline
holder_pid=31549 drain_rc=0
stdout: WAKE DRAIN SKIPPED: queue lock remains held by live pid 31549 after 1s; retry on the next drain.
stderr: 
queue unchanged: yes
### S-malformed-queue-lock: a regular file sits where the queue lock dir belongs
drain_rc=1
stdout: 
stderr: wake drain: queue lock could not be acquired safely
malformed lock left in place: yes
### S-holder-releases-in-window: the holder releases inside the deadline, drain then gets the rows
drain_rc=0 rows_replayed=3
WAKE_ACK_REQUIRED: after handling completes run bin/fm-wake-drain.sh --ack-through 3 --recovery-generation <gen>
### S-ack-stays-blocking: an acknowledgement waits for a live holder (no deadline), then consumes
ack_rc=0 waited_secs=4 (holder held 4s, presentation timeout 1s)
queue empty after ack: yes
